docs/testing/aci_vmstate/build/

# A checker must not write into the tree it checks: a tracked stamp file here
# dirtied the shared checkout and dispatcher.sh refuses to build on a dirty
# tree, so a guard stalled 129 builds. The high-water mark is derived from git
# history now; this line is belt-and-braces.
docs/testing/.territory_wave

# The OWNER'S OWN ES-DE configuration, pulled from the device for reference
# when this branch's launcher bug was worked. 25 systems and 37 emulators --
# their real library layout and emulator set, which is personal data and must
# not be committed. It is NOT the same file as docs/es-de/es_systems.xml, which
# is our minimal single-system version for distribution (1 system, 1 emulator).
#
# Kept locally rather than deleted, because they are the owner's files and they
# document what ES-DE actually expects of us. Ignored because a `git add -A`
# here would publish them: this session ran one, and only caught it because it
# also swept in 44 agent worktrees and produced a wall of warnings. These two
# would have gone in silently.
es_find_rules.xml
es_systems.xml
